  "title": "Markdown to PDF Converter – Free MD to PDF Online | Digitum",
  "desc": "Convert markdown to PDF online with selectable text, clickable links, highlighted code, tables and maths. A free markdown to PDF converter, no sign-up.",
  "eyebrow": "Markdown to PDF",
  "h1": "Convert Markdown to PDF that <em>looks the part</em>",
  "lede": "Turn markdown to PDF in a few clicks: open or paste your document and save a clean, print-ready file. Text stays selectable, links stay clickable, and code, tables and maths are properly formatted.",
  "content": "<h2>Why convert markdown to PDF?</h2>\n<p>Markdown is ideal for writing, but not everyone you work with has a markdown viewer. A PDF opens the same way on every computer and phone, prints predictably and cannot be edited by accident. That makes it the usual choice for reports, proposals, CVs and handouts that start life as a .md file.</p>\n<p>This markdown to PDF converter uses your browser's own print engine rather than taking a picture of the page. The result is a real document: you can search it, copy text out of it and click its links. Headings, lists, tables and blockquotes keep their formatting, code blocks keep their syntax colours, and LaTeX maths is rendered with KaTeX before printing.</p>\n<p>You stay in control of the layout. Choose A4 or Letter paper, narrow, normal or wide margins and page numbers in Settings, or add your own CSS to change fonts and colours. To convert markdown to PDF on a phone, use the share or print menu and choose Save as PDF. If you need an editable file instead, try <a href=\"/markdown-to-word\">Markdown to Word</a>, and to go the other way use <a href=\"/pdf-to-markdown\">PDF to Markdown</a>.</p>\n<p>The PDF always uses the light print layout, even if you read in dark mode, and the app's toolbars are left out.</p>\n<h2>A PDF worth sending</h2>\n<div class=\"feats\"><div class=\"feat\"><h3>Real text, not a screenshot</h3><p>The PDF is made by your browser&#x27;s own print engine, so text can be selected and searched, and links can be clicked.</p></div><div class=\"feat\"><h3>Paper, margins and page numbers</h3><p>Pick A4 or Letter, narrow, normal or wide margins, and page numbers at the foot of each page in Settings.</p></div><div class=\"feat\"><h3>Code, tables and maths</h3><p>Syntax-highlighted code blocks, tables that do not break across pages where they can avoid it, and LaTeX maths rendered with KaTeX.</p></div><div class=\"feat\"><h3>Always light and clean</h3><p>Even if you read in dark mode, the PDF comes out in the light print layout, without the app&#x27;s buttons and panels.</p></div><div class=\"feat\"><h3>Your own styling</h3><p>Add custom CSS in Settings to change fonts, colours or spacing in the PDF.</p></div><div class=\"feat\"><h3>Private</h3><p>The conversion happens on your device. Nothing is uploaded.</p></div></div>\n<h2>How to convert Markdown to PDF</h2>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Drag your .md file onto the page, or paste markdown into the box below.</li><li>Optionally set paper size, margins and page numbers in <strong>Settings</strong>.</li><li>Press the <strong>Export</strong> button and choose <strong>PDF</strong>.</li><li>In the print dialog, choose <strong>Save as PDF</strong> as the destination and save.</li></ol>\n<h2>Common uses for an MD to PDF converter</h2>\n<ul class=\"uses\"><li>Sending a project README or spec to a client who does not use GitHub.</li><li>Printing lecture notes or study guides written in markdown.</li><li>Turning a markdown CV into a PDF for job applications.</li><li>Archiving meeting notes or decision records in a format that will not change.</li><li>Sharing a technical write-up with maths and code samples as one tidy file.</li><li>Attaching a formatted report to an email instead of a raw .md file.</li></ul>\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<div class=\"faq\">\n<details><summary>How do I convert an MD file to PDF?</summary><p>Open the .md file here, press Export, choose PDF, then pick Save as PDF in the print dialog. The file is named after your document.</p></details>\n<details><summary>Will links work in the PDF?</summary><p>Yes. Links stay clickable and text stays selectable, because the PDF is produced from the formatted page rather than from an image.</p></details>\n<details><summary>Can I add page numbers?</summary><p>Yes. Turn on Page numbers in Settings, under PDF and print, and each page gets a number at the bottom.</p></details>\n<details><summary>Is there a file size limit?</summary><p>No. The conversion runs in your browser, so very long documents work too.</p></details>\n<details><summary>Can I export to other formats?</summary><p>Yes: Markdown, plain HTML, styled HTML and PNG are in the same Export menu.</p></details>\n<details><summary>What is the quickest way to convert MD to PDF?</summary><p>Open the .md file, press Export, choose PDF and pick Save as PDF as the destination. There is nothing to install and no account, and the file is created on your own device.</p></details>\n</div>\n<h2>Related markdown tools</h2>\n<nav class=\"tools related\" aria-label=\"Related tools\"><a href=\"/markdown-to-html\"><strong>Markdown to HTML</strong><span>Clean or styled, self-contained HTML</span></a><a href=\"/markdown-to-word\"><strong>Markdown to Word</strong><span>A real .docx with Word styles</span></a><a href=\"/markdown-to-google-docs\"><strong>Markdown to Google Docs</strong><span>Paste formatted into a doc</span></a><a href=\"/markdown-to-excel\"><strong>Markdown to Excel</strong><span>Tables to an .xlsx workbook</span></a><a href=\"/markdown-to-csv\"><strong>Markdown to CSV</strong><span>Extract tables as CSV</span></a><a href=\"/markdown-to-image\"><strong>Markdown to Image</strong><span>PNG or JPG in light or dark</span></a><a href=\"/markdown-to-text\"><strong>Markdown to Text</strong><span>Strip the syntax, keep the words</span></a><a href=\"/markdown-to-epub\"><strong>Markdown to EPUB</strong><span>Build an ebook from markdown</span></a></nav>\n<p><a class=\"all-link\" href=\"/tools\">See all 41 free markdown tools →</a></p>",
